<header class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Built by someone who lived it.</h1>
    <p>Future Operating Base exists because one veteran got out, had no idea what she didn't know, and decided nobody else should have to find out the hard way either.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="about-block">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-photo"><img src="headshot.jpg" alt="Catherine Resoco, Founder"></div>
      <div>
        <h2>The founder</h2>
        <p>I'm a Marine Corps veteran. When I got out, I didn't know what I'd earned, who to ask, or where to even start looking — and I don't think that's unusual. It's the default experience.</p>
        <p>I built Future Operating Base myself, largely through AI-assisted development. I'm not a trained engineer, and I'm not pretending to be one. I'm someone who needed this tool, so I built it — learning as I went, and staying honest about the fact that it's still a work in progress.</p>
        <p>It's free. It's staying free. And it's still very much in progress — which is exactly why your feedback matters right now, while it's still being shaped.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="about-block alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="about-grid reverse">
      <div>
        <h2>Why it exists</h2>
        <p>Transitioning out of the military means untangling GI Bill vs. VR&amp;E, home loan eligibility, disability claims, and a separation timeline — usually spread across six different offices, each speaking its own dialect of acronym.</p>
        <p>You don't have a benefits problem. You have an information problem. Future Operating Base exists to put the plain-language version of all of it in one place, personalized to your actual EAS date and branch.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-photo"><img src="logo.png" alt="" style="background:var(--vivid); padding:60px; aspect-ratio:1/1; object-fit:contain;"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="about-block">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>What we stand for</h2>
    <div class="values-row">
      <div class="value-card">
        <h3>Free, always</h3>
        <p>Future Operating Base is free to use today and will stay free. Funding comes from grants and strategic investment — never from the people using it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card">
        <h3>Independent</h3>
        <p>This is not affiliated with or endorsed by the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs. It's an independent resource built to help you navigate the system that exists.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="value-card">
        <h3>Plain language</h3>
        <p>Every source is a real regulation or official benefit — translated out of bureaucratic language, not simplified into something inaccurate.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

